{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Moses was eighty years old.</b> Despite their old age, they hastened and were zealous to do the will of their Maker. For indeed one who reached eighty, even in those days, had already passed the days of old age and arrived at advanced strength, as he testified in his prayer, saying: יְמֵי שְׁנוֹתֵינוּ בָהֶם שִׁבְעִים שָׁנָה וְגוֹ' (Psalms 90:10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "גבורות (literally 'strengths') rendered as 'advanced strength,' following the idiom from Psalms 90:10 which Sforno cites; the term refers to the life-stage beyond seventy, not to youthful vigor."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:41.726914058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}